CORE
test.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model A:observe_A --nondet-volatile-write-model B:observe_B --mmio-weak --mmio-weak-depth 1
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
a write to A observed before GO: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
With a depth-1 posted-write buffer (the default), the second write to A forces
the first to be observed, so a write to A is always observed before the command
and the property holds. The deeper reordering that violates it requires
--mmio-weak-depth 2 (see test.desc).
